# NOTE ON FORMAT (verified against Spectrum's native SS/CsVendor/SDN_INTEG/
# AppNetaAdmin/AlertMap, e.g. its apnSqEvent block): each inline "# name"
# comment labels the OID/attribute-id pair on the FOLLOWING line, not the
# one it's attached below. The trailing word on a trap's header line (e.g.
# "alarmDescription" below) labels that trap's FIRST varbind line, which
# has no comment of its own.
#
# Two trap codes per family: the "Alarm" tier (Minor/Major/Critical) maps to an
# EventDisp "A" directive on the same code; the "Event" tier (Warning) is a bare
# code with no EventDisp action, so it is logged only. alarm_bridge/mapping.py
# selects the tier before the trap is sent.


